{
 "$comment": "Curated space sites the GeoNames gazetteer lacks or names only in the local language: launch sites, spaceports, space centres, mission control, deep-space and ground stations, space-surveillance radars. lon/lat in decimal degrees (WGS84), from published site coordinates; 'code' selects the FEATURE_CODE/FEATURE_NAME pair in build-space-sites-shard.mjs. Keep one row per site, English name first, local or common aliases in 'ascii'. Every coordinate was checked 2026-09-14 against published pad/facility positions (Wikipedia infoboxes, agency pages, OSM); owner rule: the surveyed pad or facility centre, never the town. Prince Albert, Sonmiani and Poker Flat have only coarse published values. Imported from SpaceAware-UI e0d053f. Wikidata items (wikidata) were matched 2026-10-13 by tools/match-register-qids.mjs and reviewed by hand: same name, the item's class a launch site, spaceport, space centre, ground station or test facility, and its coordinate within 5 km (or none); items typed as a settlement were left out. A site with an item takes the item's position (P625) and lifecycle each run. status/statusDate/statusUrl: a lifecycle the item does not state, with the page that states it (Hammaguir: France left in 1967; ELA-3: Ariane 5's last flight, 2023-07-05). 2026-10-13 (owner: \"It should all load over SDN\"): the GeoNames space-centre, satellite-station and launch placemarks the console bundled are rows here (geonames: the placemark id; position and name from GeoNames, CC BY 4.0); placemarks that duplicate a row (Kennedy, Guiana, Esrange, Marshall, Naro, Tanegashima, Haleakala), mislabelled ones (television transmitters, businesses, a museum rocket) and one with a wrong position (Vikram Sarabhai, placed in Pune) are not. page: the row's English Wikipedia article (en:Title), its own page when the row has no item (titles and links only).",
 "codes": {
  "S.LNCH": "launch site",
  "S.SPRT": "spaceport",
  "S.CTRS": "space center",
  "S.MCC": "mission control center",
  "S.DSS": "deep space station",
  "S.STNS": "satellite ground station",
  "S.SSA": "space surveillance site",
  "S.TEST": "rocket test site"
 },
